<section class="section" aria-labelledby="consistency-heading">
  <div class="split reveal">
    <div class="split-text">
      <span class="sect-label">Character Consistency</span>
      <h2 id="consistency-heading">AI Characters That Stay <span class="grad-text">Consistent Shot to Shot</span></h2>
      <p>When you prompt Kling or Runway directly, your character&rsquo;s face shifts between takes. 10zebra&rsquo;s image-first reference pipeline locks it.</p>
      <ul class="feat-list">
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Reference portraits</strong> &mdash; generate a character image once, then anchor every subsequent shot to it automatically.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Character Swap</strong> &mdash; drop in a reference photo to replace the person in any video while preserving all original motion.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Environment locking</strong> &mdash; maintain lighting, color palette, and art direction across your whole storyboard.</span></li>
        <li><span class="check-icon">&#10003;</span> <span><strong>Multi-reference editing</strong> &mdash; blend up to 3 references (character, costume, environment) into a single new frame.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
